 CROSS-SECTION EVALUATION PROCEDURE                               2631 1451   87
                                                                  2631 1451   88
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                2631 1451   89
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               2631 1451   90
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             2631 1451   91
                                                                  2631 1451   92
 This code integrates into a single system a number               2631 1451   93
 of important modules and features:                               2631 1451   94
                                                                  2631 1451   95
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 2631 1451   96
   coupled-channels code ECIS06 by J. Raynal                      2631 1451   97
 - Soft-rotator deformed Optical Model including                  2631 1451   98
   coupled-channels code OPTMAN by E.Soukhovitskii                2631 1451   99
   and coworkers                                                  2631 1451  100
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    2631 1451  101
   width fluctuation correction, and the                          2631 1451  102
   optical model for fission with partial damping                 2631 1451  103
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                2631 1451  104
   TRISTAN by H.Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                       2631 1451  105
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      2631 1451  106
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 2631 1451  107
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                2631 1451  108
 - Hybrid Monte Carlo preequilibrium model(M.Blann)               2631 1451  109
   (code DDHMS by M.Chadwick, mod. by B.V.Carlson)                2631 1451  110
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   2631 1451  111
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                2631 1451  112
   discrete transitions                                           2631 1451  113
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                2631 1451  114
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                2631 1451  115
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               2631 1451  116
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 2631 1451  117
   library [RIPL]                                                 2631 1451  118
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              2631 1451  119
   EXFOR library                                                  2631 1451  120
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A.Trkov)                     2631 1451  121
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 2631 1451  122
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                2631 1451  123
   PrePro codes by D. Cullen                                      2631 1451  124
 - ENDF checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                   2631 1451  125
 - Highly automated fitting of optical model                      2631 1451  126
   parameters (by B.V. Carlson)                                   2631 1451  127
 - KALMAN code for fitting experimental data and                  2631 1451  128
 - generating covariances                                         2631 1451  129
 - Support for NJOY                                               2631 1451  130
